      "body": "## Summary\n\nFixes #42745.\n\n`apply_top_k_top_p_pytorch` uses an in-place `scatter_` to restore sorted logits to their original positions:\n\n```python\nreturn logits.scatter_(dim=-1, index=logits_idx, src=logits_sort)\n```\n\nIn-place ops on captured tensors are banned during CUDA graph capture, raising:\n\n```\ntorch.AcceleratorError: CUDA error: operation not permitted\n# ... in apply_top_k_top_p_pytorch\n    logits.scatter_(dim=-1, index=logits_idx, src=logits_sort)\n```\n\nThis affects any device where FlashInfer's JIT-time arch detection rejects the architecture (e.g. Blackwell GB10, `sm_121a`) and vLLM falls back to the PyTorch-native sampler while cudagraph capture is active. The resulting `EngineCoreError` cascades to 500s on all subsequent requests.\n\n## Fix\n\nReplace in-place `scatter_` with out-of-place `scatter`:\n\n```python\nreturn logits.scatter(dim=-1, index=logits_idx, src=logits_sort)\n```\n\nSince `logits_idx` from `logits.sort()` is a permutation that covers every column index, the out-of-place semantics are identical — and the returned tensor is safe to use under cudagraph capture.\n\n## Tests\n\nAdded `tests/v1/sample/test_topk_topp_scatter_cudagraph.py`:\n- Verifies the result is a **new tensor** (not an alias of `logits`)\n- Verifies `logits` is **not modified in-place**\n- Verifies top-k keeps exactly `k` finite logits per row\n- Verifies top-p always keeps at least one finite logit per row\n- Covers combined top-k + top-p, shape preservation, and the no-op path",
      "changedFiles": 2,
